// Scrape SIP account registration status and set a labeled gauge per account.
// get_subaccounts() and get_registration_status() are siblings in this
// namespace, so they are called by their bare names.
//
// The scrape walks the sub-account ROSTER and asks about each account
// individually, rather than asking once for "everything registered" and
// setting a 1 per hit. Two reasons, and both of them were live bugs:
//
//   1. getRegistrationStatus is per-account. With no `account` parameter it
//      returns an aggregate with no `registrations` key, so the old
//      list-shaped call threw as soon as nothing was registered — the scrape
//      failed entirely at exactly the moment it had something to report.
//   2. A labeled gauge child cannot be removed once created, so a loop that
//      only ever writes 1 can never say "this account went away". Walking the
//      roster means every known account gets an explicit 1 or 0 every pass,
//      which is what makes `== 0` alerting and a "how many are registered"
//      sum possible at all.
//
// This costs one API call per account per scrape on top of the roster call.
// With a handful of accounts and the 4m interval in voipms-sip.vcl, that is
// nothing, and it is the only shape the API actually supports.
namespace voipms

func scrape_sip_accounts(ctx: ctx) {
    var accounts = get_subaccounts(ctx)

    for acct in accounts {
        var labels = {account_id = acct.account}
        var registered = 0
        if get_registration_status(ctx, acct.account) == "yes" {
            registered = 1
        }
        // Log the label set and the verdict only. `acct` holds the plaintext
        // SIP password — see the warning on get_subaccounts().
        log::info("sip_account", {labels = labels, registered = registered})
        set(metric.voipms_sipaccount_registered, registered, labels)
    }
}
